<section class="legal-section">
  <div class="dw-container">
    <div class="legal-body">

      <p>This policy explains what personal data <strong>Dadword IT</strong> collects through this website and when you work with us, why we use it, who we share it with and the rights you have. It is written to meet the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the UK GDPR and the privacy laws of the other countries where our clients are based.</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p><strong>Dadword IT</strong> is the controller of the personal data described in this policy.</p>
      <p>N-1007, North Building, Twinstar, 150 Feet Ring Road, Rajkot 360004, Gujarat, India<br>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@dadwordit.com">contact@dadwordit.com</a></p>

      <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>

      <h3>When you send us a project enquiry</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data:</strong> your name, email address, company, phone number (optional), project type, budget range and message.</li>
        <li><strong>Why:</strong> to reply to you, discuss your project and prepare a proposal.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> taking steps at your request before entering into a contract (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)) and our legitimate interest in responding to business enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f)).</li>
        <li>To protect the form from spam, your IP address is checked against a short-term limit held in our server's memory for 10 minutes. It is not stored with your enquiry.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>When you book a call</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data:</strong> your name, email address, the time you choose and anything you add to the booking.</li>
        <li><strong>Why:</strong> to schedule and hold the call. Bookings are handled by Calendly.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> steps before entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)).</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>When you email us or become a client</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data:</strong> contact details, correspondence, contracts, invoices and payment records.</li>
        <li><strong>Why:</strong> to deliver our services, manage the relationship and meet accounting and tax obligations.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)).</li>
        <li>If your project gives us access to personal data about your own users or customers, we process it only on your instructions as your processor. We can sign a data processing agreement on request.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Website analytics</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data:</strong> pages viewed, how you arrived, device and browser type, approximate location (country or city) and actions such as submitting the contact form. Google Analytics 4 does not store full IP addresses.</li>
        <li><strong>Why:</strong> to see which pages are useful and improve the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> in the EEA, UK and Switzerland, your consent (Art. 6(1)(a)). Analytics cookies are not set unless you accept them in the cookie banner. Elsewhere, our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>We do not sell your personal data, use it for advertising or make automated decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">3. Cookies</h2>
      <p>We only use the cookies and storage listed below. You can change your choice at any time with <button type="button" class="footer-cookie-btn" data-cookie-settings style="font-size:inherit;color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline">Cookie settings</button>, or delete cookies in your browser.</p>
      <div class="legal-table-wrap">
        <table class="legal-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Analytics: distinguishes visitors and sessions. Only set with consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland.</td><td>Up to 2 years</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>dwConsent</code> (browser storage)</td><td>Dadword IT</td><td>Remembers your cookie choice so we don't ask on every page.</td><td>12 months</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Calendly cookies</td><td>Calendly</td><td>Needed for the booking calendar on the Book a Call page to work. Only set on that page.</td><td>Set by Calendly</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We share personal data only with service providers that help us run the website and our business, under contracts that require them to protect it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Analytics and Google Workspace email), Ireland and USA.</li>
        <li><strong>Calendly</strong> (call scheduling), USA.</li>
        <li><strong>n8n</strong>, the workflow tool we use to route website enquiries to our inbox.</li>
        <li>Our website and server hosting provider.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose data where the law requires it, or to protect our rights in a dispute.</p>

      <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
      <p>Dadword IT is based in India, and some of our providers are in the USA. When personal data from the EEA, UK or Switzerland is transferred to these countries, we rely on the safeguards our providers offer, such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, the UK International Data Transfer Addendum or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. Data you send us directly is transferred to India because it is necessary to respond to your request or to perform a contract with you (GDPR Art. 49(1)(b)).</p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiries and bookings</strong> that do not lead to a project: up to 24 months, then deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Client records</strong>: for the length of the engagement and afterwards for as long as tax and accounting laws require.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics data</strong>: 14 months in Google Analytics.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR and UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you and get a copy;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data deleted;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to how we use it, including use based on legitimate interests;</li>
        <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, for example through Cookie settings, without affecting earlier processing;</li>
        <li>complain to your local data protection authority. In the UK this is the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Wherever you are, including the USA, Canada, Australia and the Gulf, you can ask us to access, correct or delete your personal data. Email <a href="mailto:contact@dadwordit.com">contact@dadwordit.com</a> and we will respond within one month. We may need to confirm your identity first.</p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>We protect personal data with encrypted connections (HTTPS), access limited to the people who need it, secrets kept out of public code, and spam and abuse protection on our forms. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, but we work to protect your data and will notify you and the relevant authorities of a breach where the law requires it.</p>

      <h2>9. Children</h2>
      <p>This website and our services are for businesses and are not directed at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect their personal data.</p>

      <h2>10. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>Our website links to other sites such as Upwork, Clutch and LinkedIn. Their privacy practices are their own, so please read their policies.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We will update this page when our practices or the law change, and change the date at the top. Significant changes will be highlighted on this page.</p>

      <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
      <p>For any question about this policy or your personal data:</p>
      <p><strong>Dadword IT</strong><br>N-1007, North Building, Twinstar, 150 Feet Ring Road, Rajkot 360004, Gujarat, India<br>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@dadwordit.com">contact@dadwordit.com</a></p>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

